[["heading","FULL-STACK SE INTERNSHIP PREPARATION • 03 / 34\nData Structures\nComplete Interview Edition"],["heading","31 lessons • Sinhala + English • Java examples"],["sinhala","","A data structure organizes data for efficient access and modification. Data පහසුJවෙන් store,",454],["sinhala","","search, update සහ delete කරන්න සංවිධානය කරන ක්‍රමයක්.",312],["text","Lessons 1–12 follow the original master checklist, page 1, Section 03. Lessons 13–31 are"],["text","supplemental topics selected for broader internship preparation. Algorithm details continue in"],["text","Section 04."],["text","Java snippets are independent. Use import java.util.*; where required. Put executable"],["text","statements inside main; class and method declarations belong in an appropriate class context."],["text","Examples assume modern Java."],["heading","Contents"],["text","1. Arrays"],["text","17. Circular queues / ring buffers"],["text","2. Strings"],["text","18. Hash functions and collisions"],["text","3. Linked lists (singly and doubly)"],["text","19. Load factor and rehashing"],["text","4. Stacks"],["text","20. Ordered maps and sets"],["text","5. Queues and deques"],["text","21. Tree terminology and types"],["text","6. Hash maps and hash sets"],["text","22. Tree traversals"],["text","7. Trees and binary search trees"],["text","23. Balanced trees (AVL and Red-Black)"],["text","8. Heaps and priority queues"],["text","24. B-trees and B+ trees"],["text","9. Graphs"],["text","25. Graph types and terminology"],["text","10. Adjacency lists and matrices"],["text","26. BFS and DFS data structures"],["text","11. Tries (extra)"],["text","27. Disjoint set / Union-Find"],["text","12. Choosing a suitable data structure"],["text","28. Bitsets"],["text","13. Abstract data types (ADT)"],["text","29. Java Collections Framework"],["text","14. Dynamic arrays / ArrayList"],["text","30. Comparable and Comparator"],["text","15. Multidimensional arrays"],["text","31. Time and space complexity of structures"],["text","16. Circular linked lists"]]